{"pages":[{"w":612.0,"h":792.0,"s":[[13.889,2.206,18.17,3.8,3.431,"EQUINOX"],[13.889,5.306,14.953,1.205,1.078,"Q U A N T I T A T I V E"],[69.444,2.807,15.359,1.643,1.471,"India Equity Research"],[69.444,4.27,11.266,1.46,1.307,"20 November 2026"],[13.889,10.995,23.136,3.651,3.268,"Ashok Leyland"],[13.889,14.731,30.841,2.373,2.124,"Record volumes, thinner margins"],[13.889,20.845,52.936,1.809,1.634,"Neutral, Dec-27 target ₹165. Q2 FY27 (out on Saturday 14 November) brought"],[13.889,22.289,52.951,1.809,1.634,"record volumes of 64,677 vehicles (+32%) and revenue up 39% to ₹13,364 cr,"],[13.889,23.733,52.934,1.809,1.634,"but EBITDA rose only 16%: the margin fell to 10.1% from 12.1% as materials"],[13.889,25.177,52.957,1.809,1.634,"took 74.9% of revenue against 71.2%. The shares are 1.8% lower since (NIFTY"],[13.889,26.621,52.931,1.809,1.634,"+1.5%) and 22% below February’s high, yet the price still assumes recovery: on"],[13.889,28.065,52.931,1.809,1.634,"cash flow alone it needs a 14.8% EBITDA margin through the cycle, above"],[13.889,29.509,14.563,1.809,1.634,"FY26’s record 13.0%."],[13.889,31.995,52.934,1.809,1.634,"1) Management called Q2 the peak for input costs and has raised truck prices"],[13.889,33.439,52.934,1.809,1.634,"about 2.25% since April. We have the H2 margin at 12.6% (14.0% a year ago)"],[13.889,34.883,52.934,1.809,1.634,"on revenue up 11% against a base the GST cut lifted; October domestic volumes"],[13.889,36.328,52.961,1.809,1.634,"rose 24%. FY27E EPS of ₹6.60 is 3% above consensus, which has H2 EPS"],[13.889,37.772,52.951,1.809,1.634,"down 6%. 2) H1 operating cash flow was ₹87 cr negative as payables unwound."],[13.889,39.216,52.931,1.809,1.634,"3) The auditors disclaimed their conclusion on the consolidated results: Hinduja"],[13.889,40.684,52.951,1.809,1.634,"Leyland Finance (HLF), the 61%-owned lender with ₹70,403 cr of assets,"],[13.889,42.128,52.931,1.809,1.634,"cannot reconcile loan balances across its systems. FY28E EPS grows 24% as the"],[13.889,43.572,16.309,1.809,1.634,"margin returns to 12.8%."],[13.889,46.034,52.964,1.809,1.634,"The target adds two parts. The truck business averages its own three-year P/E of"],[13.889,47.502,52.931,1.809,1.634,"20.5x on Dec-27 forward EPS (₹180) and a ten-year DCF at 12% with the"],[13.889,48.946,52.934,1.809,1.634,"margin settling at 12%, plus net cash (₹127); the DCF is lower because it does"],[13.889,50.39,52.931,1.809,1.634,"not assume FY26’s peak margin lasts. HLF counts at one times book (₹9 a"],[13.889,51.834,52.934,1.809,1.634,"share); it merges into listed NDL Ventures, leaving Ashok Leyland 59.6%. Other"],[13.889,53.278,52.931,1.809,1.634,"subsidiaries count at nil. What would prove us wrong: a Q4 margin back above"],[13.889,54.722,52.931,1.809,1.634,"14%, or NDL valued well above book (1.5 times adds ₹5). Risks: H2 demand"],[13.889,56.167,47.038,1.809,1.634,"against the GST-led base; a write-down at HLF after its systems review."],[13.889,58.654,13.042,1.643,1.471,"Price Performance"],[15.268,67.265,1.489,1.022,0.915,"100"],[15.268,64.904,1.489,1.022,0.915,"150"],[15.268,62.554,1.489,1.022,0.915,"200"],[15.268,60.195,1.489,1.022,0.915,"250"],[17.994,67.96,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Jan 26"],[22.621,67.96,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Apr 26"],[27.408,67.96,2.47,1.022,0.915,"Jul 26"],[32.161,67.96,2.96,1.022,0.915,"Oct 26"],[17.044,69.131,6.431,1.275,1.111,"Ashok Leyland ("],[23.478,69.157,0.618,1.241,1.111,"₹"],[24.091,69.131,0.303,1.275,1.111,")"],[27.175,69.131,7.901,1.275,1.111,"NIFTY 50 (rebased)"],[20.099,70.291,1.972,1.387,1.209,"YTD"],[25.13,70.291,1.433,1.387,1.209,"1m"],[30.516,70.291,1.433,1.387,1.209,"3m"],[34.446,70.291,1.984,1.387,1.209,"12m"],[15.277,71.356,1.691,1.387,1.209,"Abs"],[19.149,71.356,2.842,1.387,1.209,"−5.7%"],[23.66,71.356,2.811,1.387,1.209,"12.5%"],[29.015,71.356,2.842,1.387,1.209,"−4.0%"],[33.527,71.356,2.811,1.387,1.209,"16.2%"],[15.492,72.421,1.476,1.387,1.209,"Rel"],[19.149,72.421,2.842,1.387,1.209,"−3.3%"],[24.211,72.421,2.26,1.387,1.209